# Build output. Regenerated by build.sh from Source.
#
# The zip is listed separately because *.pdx does not match Spindle.pdx.zip,
# which is how a release asset ended up committed once. Releases carry the zip;
# the repository does not need a copy of its own build output.
*.pdx
*.pdx.zip

# macOS clutter.
.DS_Store

# Python leaves these behind whenever ingest.py is imported rather than run.
__pycache__/

# The generated library is not tracked. It is hundreds of megabytes of
# converted audio produced by tools/ingest.py from your own music, and it does
# not belong in version control. Regenerate it with:
#     python3 tools/ingest.py <music folder> <output folder>
build/
library/

# Source music, if anyone ever puts it inside the project folder.
Music/

# Everything below is kept locally and deliberately not published. None of it is
# needed to build Spindle, run it, or prepare music for it, which is the bar for
# being in the repository at all.

# The two Roobert fonts, copied out of the Playdate SDK by build.sh before every
# compile. They are Panic's to license, not mine, so they cannot sit in a
# repository that hands everything to everyone under 0BSD. Every Playdate
# developer already has the SDK, so copying them at build time costs nobody
# anything.
Source/fonts/

# The copy of ingest.py that ships inside the app, so a device with no music can
# hand you the tool that fixes that. build.sh copies it in from tools/ before
# every compile, and one copy in the repository is what stops the shipped tool
# and the real one drifting apart.
Source/docs/ingest.py

# The social banner. Generated by make_launcher_art.py and uploaded by hand
# under Settings, Social preview. Nothing in the repository reads it, so nothing
# in the repository needs to carry it.
docs/social-banner.png

# The design document. A working document rather than something to publish.
DESIGN.md

# Raw logs from the hardware investigation. Useful to me, noise to anyone else,
# and some of them are named after other people's projects because their files
# were used as test material.
notes/

# The tooling that makes the demo video and the animations. Promotional work
# rather than part of the app.
tools/demo-recorder/
tools/make_demo_video.py
tools/make_readme_animations.py
